# Deny everything, then admit only what the image is built from.
#
# An allow-list rather than a deny-list because the two failure modes are not
# symmetric. A gap in a deny-list ships .env.local — real API keys — into an
# image that gets pushed to a public registry, and nothing fails. A gap here
# fails the build loudly on the next line.

*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!src

# Re-admitting src/ brings whatever is sitting in it, and a host __pycache__
# holds macOS-built bytecode that would shadow the image's own.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
